// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  The Foreign Exchange — a Rholang program that ships a λ-calculus Foreign Language Term,
//  destructures it with typed holes, and reconstructs it, all on the f1r3node Rholang reducer.
//
//  Run me with the Rholang interpreter:
//    rholang demos/flt-foreign-exchange/foreign-exchange.rho
//
//  FOREIGN LANGUAGE TERMS ARE A RHOLANG GRAMMAR FEATURE
//  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Rholang (MeTTaIL's Rholang-1.4 surface) can carry a term of ANOTHER language verbatim. The
//  opener `lambda:Term`…`` embeds a guest term written in the untyped λ-calculus; the text between the
//  back-ticks is the guest's OWN concrete syntax, which Rholang hands to the guest's reflector
//  (secure by construction — No-Injection). The interpreter bundles the `lambda` guest, so this is
//  ordinary Rholang — nothing about the interpreter is FLT-specific.
//
//  THE PROGRAM
//  ───────────
//        flt!( lambda:Term`(lam x. x, lam a. lam b. a)` )                    // ship App(I, K) on flt
//        | for( @lambda:Term`(${f}, ${k})` <- flt ){ @"OUT"!( lambda:Term`(${f}, ${k})` ) }
//
//  The FLT `lambda:Term`(fun, arg)`` reflects to the guest application node App(fun, arg), with:
//        fun = lam x. x           — the identity combinator  I  (= λ.0 in de-Bruijn form)
//        arg = lam a. lam b. a    — the constant  combinator  K  (= λ.λ.1)
//  so the shipped term is App(I, K).
//
//  THE TYPED HOLES
//  ───────────────
//  The receive pattern is itself an FLT, `lambda:Term`(${f}, ${k})``, carrying two TYPED HOLES:
//        ${f}  binds the function position   ⟶   ⟦I⟧ = λ.0
//        ${k}  binds the argument position   ⟶   ⟦K⟧ = λ.λ.1
//  A `${x}` hole is a secure typed-AST hole: it matches a reflected sub-term by SHAPE, never by
//  string splicing. On the reducer the send and receive rendezvous in ONE COMM (a real Rholang
//  reduction): the holes capture the two foreign sub-terms, the body RE-QUOTES `lambda:Term`(${f}, ${k})``
//  filling the holes, and the reconstructed application is published to @"OUT".
//
//  EXPECT
//  ──────
//        @"OUT"  =  ⟦(λ.0 λ.λ.1)⟧          (App(I, K), rebuilt from the two captured holes)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

new flt in {
  flt!(lambda:Term`(lam x. x, lam a. lam b. a)`) |
  for(@lambda:Term`(${f}, ${k})` <- flt) {
    @"OUT"!(lambda:Term`(${f}, ${k})`)
  }
}
